    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0448" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3334: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-09-28T15:00:00-04:00">September 28, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. The Brazilian Minister of Foreign Affairs today informed the Bolivian
                    Government that if the ABCP is to accept the League mandate Bolivia must either
                    accept without reservation the proposal of August 25th or the Chilean suggestion
                    for a double arbitration.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d319-f1"/> It is not likely that
                    Bolivia will accept either plan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d319-f1" n="34" xml:id="d319-f1-content">
                <p>See League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official Journal</hi>, November
                    1933, p. 1590.</p>
            </note>
